### QR Feature UI Routes Tests
### Base URL: http://localhost:3000/qr

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/qr
@destinationUrl = https://www.example.com
@domain = mukhtasar.pro
@alias = my-qr-code

### 1. Create QR Code (minimal)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "{{destinationUrl}}"
}

###

### 2. Create QR Code with Custom Colors
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "{{destinationUrl}}",
  "foreground_color": "#FF0000",
  "background_color": "#FFFFFF"
}

###

### 3. Create QR Code with Frame (frame only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "{{destinationUrl}}",
  "foreground_color": "#000000",
  "background_color": "#FFFFFF",
  "frame_type": "frame_only",
  "frame_color": "#333333"
}

###

### 4. Create QR Code with Frame and Text
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "{{destinationUrl}}",
  "foreground_color": "#000000",
  "background_color": "#FFFFFF",
  "frame_type": "frame_with_text",
  "frame_text": "Scan Me!",
  "frame_color": "#333333",
  "frame_text_color": "#FFFFFF"
}

###

### 5. Create QR Code with Custom Domain and Alias
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "{{destinationUrl}}",
  "domain": "{{domain}}",
  "alias": "{{alias}}"
}

###

### 6. Create QR Code with All Options
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "{{destinationUrl}}",
  "foreground_color": "#0066CC",
  "background_color": "#F0F8FF",
  "alias": "{{alias}}",
  "domain": "{{domain}}",
  "frame_type": "frame_with_text",
  "frame_text": "Visit Our Site",
  "frame_color": "#0066CC",
  "frame_text_color": "#FFFFFF"
}

###

### 7. Test with Invalid URL (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "not-a-valid-url"
}

###

### 8. Test with Invalid Color Format (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "{{destinationUrl}}",
  "foreground_color": "red"
}

###

### 9. Test with Invalid Frame Type (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_url": "{{destinationUrl}}",
  "frame_type": "invalid_type"
}

###
